    "description": {
      "value": "<p>In ancient times, the night elves ruled an empire spanning the world, until Queen Azshara and her Highborne, delving into the arcane power of the Well of Eternity, opened the way for the Burning Legion. The War of the Ancients drove it back at the cost of the Great Sundering, which shattered the continent and scattered the elves.</p><p><strong>Night elves (Kaldorei)</strong> renounced arcane magic for a druidic society in the forests of Ashenvale; purple-skinned and 7 to 8 feet tall, they lost their immortality in the Legion's return. <strong>Nightborne (Shal'dorei)</strong> are the people of Suramar, transformed by ten thousand years behind the shield of the Nightwell; they joined the Horde after overthrowing their leaders. <strong>High elves (Quel'dorei)</strong> descend from the Highborne exiled for practicing arcane magic, who founded Quel'Thalas around the Sunwell; after the Scourge, the few who refused to drain magic from others now live among the Alliance. <strong>Blood elves (Sin'dorei)</strong> are the survivors of Quel'Thalas who learned to drain arcane energy from other creatures and joined the Horde; the Sunwell now burns again for them. <strong>Void elves (Ren'dorei)</strong> are blood elves exiled for studying the Void, taught by Alleria Windrunner to master the shadows within them in service of the Alliance.</p><p><strong>Renown.</strong> You have no starting Renown Score.</p><h3>Azeroth Elf Traits</h3><p><strong>Creature Type:</strong> Humanoid</p><p><strong>Size:</strong> Medium (about 6–8 feet tall)</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 30 feet</p><p><strong>Darkvision:</strong> 60 feet</p><p><strong>@UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.species.Item.MTlet1RoZbBOFM0N]{Elven Lineage}.</strong> Your lineage gives you its level 1 benefit, then a spell at character levels 3 and 5, each cast once per Long Rest without a spell slot (Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma).</p><p><strong>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.origins24.Item.phbsptFeyAncestr]{Fey Ancestry}.</strong> You have Advantage on saving throws you make to avoid or end the &amp;Reference[Charmed] condition.</p><p><strong>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.origins24.Item.phbsptKeenSenses]{Keen Senses}.</strong> You have proficiency in the Insight, Perception, or Survival skill.</p><p><strong>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.origins24.Item.phbsptTrance0000]{Trance}.</strong> You don't need to sleep, and magic can't put you to sleep. You can finish a Long Rest in 4 hours if you spend those hours in a trancelike meditation, during which you retain consciousness.</p><p><strong>@UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.species.Item.QjdA7JjxtaTvLo8D]{High Elf Lineage}.</strong> You know the Prestidigitation cantrip. Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can replace it with another cantrip from the Wizard spell list. Your spellcasting ability for it is the one you chose for this lineage.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
